      "writtenOn": "2018-08-15T14:35:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My original comment got off on SRC vs SNK.\n\nReading the spec again, I don\u0027t think that there should be a conditional on the previous task_state. If we send a source cap and it is acked (with a GoodCRC via res \u003e\u003d 0) then we should transition into the PD_STATE_SRC_NEGOCIATE state which waits for a Request message from the SNK otherwise will perform a hard reset.\n\n\"Once a Source_Capabilities Message has been received and acknowledged by a GoodCRC Message, the Sink is required to then send a Request Message within tSenderResponse.\" from 8.3.3.2.3\nPE_SRC_Send_Capabilities State",
      "parentUuid": "b2bbe744_a399b874",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1516,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 1516,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "dcb671d1a86b1fc566958b560593d1cce9810961",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
